            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0552" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12511: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-08T11:00:00+08:00">November 8, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 7—11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>841. Following from Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 7, 5 p.m. I have received information believed to be reliable
                            that the anti-communist campaign in Kiangsi was abandoned November 5th.
                            Reason assigned by my informant was pro-communist sentiment among
                            Government troops and general unwillingness to fight.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
